    "Result": "Why do wild geese change homes?Wild geese have busy lives. They fly from one place to another. They change homes twice every year. In spring they fly north. In autumn they fly south. Why do wild geese move around so much in winter? They cannot find enough food in the north, so they fly south in autumn, then in spring it is warm in the north, so they fly back.",
